														For the more experienced members of the guild, perhaps some Raid tips may be in order, so that when the web page comes about, the combined knowledge of the guild can be shared with new or current members easily. <br />
<br />
Feel free to add your thoughts here, so that the posts are centralized into one thread for ease of finding information.<br />
<br />
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~<br />
<br />
Planning - In most cases, Raids are formal. The Place &amp; Time for the raid is chosen in advance so that those whom plan to attend can make arrangements to arrive at said place when the event is to occur.<br />
<br />
The Tip is, if you show any interest whatsoever, even the slightest, in attending, please find a way to be /camped at the site of the raid in advance, such as the night before, even if you decide that you cannot make it. That way, even if you are late logging in, that you are available at the zone-in or somewhere easily accessable. Nothing is more annoying to raid organizers who've planned the raid for a week or more in advance to have to hold the show for one or more persons who are out in the middle of nowhere attempting to make it to said raid location fifteen to an hour after the raid was to start. <br />
<br />
A teacher of mine said that being right on time was actually being late. Being 5 minutes early for an appointment was being on time. This phenomenon is true for raids; being an hour or two early for a raid is on time, such as in the case for Dragon/God/UberMob raids where a buffing period is staged.						</td>
