														This was posted on one of the sites that we n have linked and is required reading: <br />
<br />
Raid Tips <br />
7/21/2001 - 10:34 PM PST <br />
---------------------------------------------------------------- <br />
Gloomer Pestalance <br />
Carven <br />
I came across this article a few weeks ago on Everlore.com. I n thought it had a few good pointers and shoud be posted. Tell n what you think. BTW this was writen by Yappie. <br />
<br />
I went to Perma for a big raid on vox yesterday, as scheduled on Everlore. There were 58 people in the zone waiting to kill her - crazy! <br />
<br />
The attack was a bust, not due to lack of offense (we sure had n enough of it!) but due to lack of leadership, coordination, and listening skills. The problem was so bad last night that I wanted to post a few tips on how to be successful on a raid, especially if it's your first time. This should be useful to a Lot of people, since many many people have high level characters now but not all of them have gone on raids, and even fewer have gone on GOOD raids <br />
<br />
QUIT ASKING QUESTIONS AND LISTEN TO THE RAID LEADER! <br />
<br />
We lost 30 people last night because ONE person didn't want to listen to the raid leader and sat too close to vox while we were organizing buffing stations. Boom he pulled her while all the n groups were disbanded. <br />
<br />
What I've learned about pick-up raids (raids where no one majority guild is leading it) is that there has to be some organization and EVERYBODY has to follow orders to the letter. Sort of like the military. You know, don't think - do and don't ask questions.						</td>
